  "notes": "THE DEMONSTRATION THAT THE TETHER IS THE FIX. Went from 0.0 percent to 87.9 percent usable EEG after an arm C swap and nothing else: hum 916.9 to 133.2 uV, spectral slope -0.38 to -2.05, railing 29.7 to 0.0 percent, with its implant untouched. Tethered at day 8 after surgery, which is why long post-operative recovery is not required for a usable recording. \u26a0\ufe0f A 40-sweep impedance block taken just after the swap said the swap had HARMED this animal, p = 8.4e-08. The block spanned 21 minutes and caught one long open state. The recording reversed it completely. This is the origin of the rule that impedance blocks screen and only a multi-hour recording is an outcome.\n",
